IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `it-types`
IMPORT `it-residence`
IMPORT `it-liability`
IMPORT `it-credits`
IMPORT `it-codes`
IMPORT `it-goal`

-- Income Tax Act 2007, personal income tax — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the Act's text. Table 1 for
-- 2026-27 is built from the thresholds the Act quotes ($15,600, $53,500,
-- $78,100, $180,000) with the rates 0.105, 0.175, 0.30, 0.33 and 0.39.

§ `Tests`

table MEANS LIST (Band OF JUST 15600, 0.105), (Band OF JUST 53500, 0.175), (Band OF JUST 78100, 0.30), (Band OF JUST 180000, 0.33), (Band OF NOTHING, 0.39)

§§ `Schedule 1 tax`

#ASSERT `the tax under table 1 on` 0 `, bands` table EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the tax under table 1 on` 15600 `, bands` table EQUALS 1638
#ASSERT `the tax under table 1 on` 15600.99 `, bands` table EQUALS 1638
#ASSERT `the tax under table 1 on` 50000 `, bands` table EQUALS 7658
#ASSERT `the tax under table 1 on` 53500 `, bands` table EQUALS 8270.5
#ASSERT `the tax under table 1 on` 100000 `, bands` table EQUALS 22877.5
#ASSERT `the tax under table 1 on` 180000 `, bands` table EQUALS 49277.5
#ASSERT `the tax under table 1 on` 200000 `, bands` table EQUALS 57077.5

§§ `Liability (ss BC 1-BC 7)`

GIVEN filing IS A BOOLEAN, withheld IS A NUMBER, income IS A NUMBER, deductions IS A NUMBER, loss IS A NUMBER, schedular IS A NUMBER, schedularTax IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Tax year facts`
year filing withheld income deductions loss schedular schedularTax MEANS
    `Tax year facts` OF 2027, filing, withheld, income, deductions, loss, schedular, schedularTax, table

#ASSERT `the net income for` (year TRUE 0 60000 5000 0 0 0) EQUALS 55000
#ASSERT `the taxable income for` (year TRUE 0 60000 5000 2000 0 0) EQUALS 53000
#ASSERT `the net income for` (year TRUE 0 10000 15000 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the net loss for` (year TRUE 0 10000 15000 0 0 0) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the net loss for` (year TRUE 0 60000 5000 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the taxable income for` (year TRUE 0 60000 5000 70000 0 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the income tax liability for` (year TRUE 0 55000 5000 0 0 0) EQUALS 7658
#ASSERT `the income tax liability for` (year FALSE 5000 55000 5000 0 0 0) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the income tax liability for` (year TRUE 0 10000 15000 0 0 0) EQUALS 0
-- BC 7: $10,000 of schedular income carrying $1,050 is taken out of the
-- $60,000; the remaining $50,000 is taxed under table 1.
#ASSERT `the income tax liability for` (year TRUE 0 60000 0 0 10000 1050) EQUALS 8708

§§ `Independent earner tax credit (ss LC 13-LC 15)`

GIVEN benefit IS A BOOLEAN, months IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Independent earner facts`
ie benefit months MEANS `Independent earner facts` OF benefit, FALSE, FALSE, months, 121, 244

#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 50000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 520
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 23999 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 24000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 520
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 66000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 520
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 66000.99 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 520
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 67000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 390
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 70000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 80000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 6) `, net income` 50000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 260
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie TRUE 12) `, net income` 50000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 50000 `, tax year ending` 2027 `, resident` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- 2024-25: 121 days to 30 July 2024 and 244 days from 31 July.
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 40000 `, tax year ending` 2025 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 520
#ASSERT `the independent earner tax credit for` (ie FALSE 12) `, net income` 50000 `, tax year ending` 2025 `, resident` TRUE EQUALS 520 TIMES 244 DIVIDED BY 365

§§ `Using credits (ss BC 8, LA 2-LA 7)`

GIVEN nonref IS A NUMBER, imputation IS A NUMBER, paye IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Credits
credits nonref imputation paye MEANS Credits OF nonref, 0, imputation, paye, 0, 0

#ASSERT `the use of credits against` 7658 `, credits` (credits 0 0 8000) `, independent earner tax credit` 520 EQUALS `Credit outcome` OF 0, 862, 0, 0, 0
#ASSERT `the use of credits against` 7658 `, credits` (credits 0 0 7000) `, independent earner tax credit` 0 EQUALS `Credit outcome` OF 658, 0, 0, 0, 0
#ASSERT `the use of credits against` 500 `, credits` (credits 1000 0 300) `, independent earner tax credit` 0 EQUALS `Credit outcome` OF 0, 300, 500, 0, 0
#ASSERT `the use of credits against` 1000 `, credits` (credits 0 1500 200) `, independent earner tax credit` 0 EQUALS `Credit outcome` OF 0, 200, 0, 0, 500
#ASSERT `the use of credits against` 1000 `, credits` (credits 300 400 200) `, independent earner tax credit` 0 EQUALS `Credit outcome` OF 100, 0, 0, 0, 0
-- LD 1(5) (added after the independent pass): a $2,000 donation credit does
-- not meet a $1,000 liability; it is refunded whole, and the liability is
-- terminal tax. A $2,000 family credit (LA 7) does meet it first.
#ASSERT `the use of credits against` 1000 `, credits` (Credits OF 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 2000) `, independent earner tax credit` 0 EQUALS `Credit outcome` OF 1000, 2000, 0, 0, 0
#ASSERT `the use of credits against` 1000 `, credits` (Credits OF 0, 0, 0, 0, 2000, 0) `, independent earner tax credit` 0 EQUALS `Credit outcome` OF 0, 1000, 0, 0, 0

§§ `Residence (ss YD 1, YD 1B)`

GIVEN abode IS A BOOLEAN, present IS A NUMBER, absent IS A NUMBER, govt IS A BOOLEAN, seasonal IS A BOOLEAN, visit IS A NUMBER, working IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Residence facts`
res abode present absent govt seasonal visit working MEANS
    `Residence facts` OF abode, present, JUST (Date 1 2 2026), absent, JUST (Date 1 1 2027), govt, seasonal, visit, visit, FALSE, working, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 184 0 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 184 0 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 2 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 184 0 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 31 1 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 183 0 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 200 0 FALSE TRUE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 200 326 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 2 2027)
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 200 326 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 31 12 2026)
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 200 325 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 2 2027)
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 200 326 TRUE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 2 2027)
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res TRUE 0 400 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 2 2027)
-- YD 1B: a 200-day visit with no work makes a non-resident visitor.
#ASSERT NOT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 200 0 FALSE FALSE 200 FALSE) `on` (Date 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 200 0 FALSE FALSE 200 TRUE) `on` (Date 1 3 2026)
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (res FALSE 276 0 FALSE FALSE 276 FALSE) `on` (Date 1 3 2026)
-- YD 1B(2)(g) (added after the independent pass): not lawfully present, so
-- not a non-resident visitor, and resident under YD 1(3).
#ASSERT `is a New Zealand resident` (`Residence facts` OF FALSE, 200, JUST (Date 1 2 2026), 0, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE, 200, 200, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) `on` (Date 1 3 2026)

§§ `Tax codes (Schedule 2)`

#ASSERT `the flat PAYE rate for the tax code` `a non-notified tax code` EQUALS 0.45
#ASSERT `the flat PAYE rate for the tax code` `S` EQUALS 0.175
#ASSERT `the flat PAYE rate for the tax code` `SA` EQUALS 0.39
#ASSERT `the flat PAYE rate for the tax code` `SB` EQUALS 0.105
#ASSERT `the flat PAYE rate for the tax code` `NSW` EQUALS 0.105
#ASSERT `the PAYE on a payment of` 1000 `under tax code` `SH` EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `the PAYE on a payment of` 1000 `under tax code` `ST` EQUALS 330
#ASSERT `the PAYE on a payment of` 1000 `under tax code` `CAE or EDW` EQUALS 175

§§ `The top-level goal`

-- A resident earning $55,000 less $5,000 deductions, with $8,000 PAYE.
#ASSERT `the tax position for` (res TRUE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `, resident on` (Date 31 3 2027) `, year` (year TRUE 0 55000 5000 0 0 0) `, credits` (credits 0 0 8000) `, independent earner facts` (ie FALSE 12) EQUALS `Tax position` OF TRUE, 55000, 50000, 0, 50000, 7658, 520, (`Credit outcome` OF 0, 862, 0, 0, 0)
#ASSERT `the tax position for` (res FALSE 0 0 FALSE FALSE 400 TRUE) `, resident on` (Date 31 3 2027) `, year` (year TRUE 0 55000 5000 0 0 0) `, credits` (credits 0 0 7000) `, independent earner facts` (ie FALSE 12) EQUALS `Tax position` OF FALSE, 55000, 50000, 0, 50000, 7658, 0, (`Credit outcome` OF 658, 0, 0, 0, 0)
